  "promptTemplate": "Use case: precise-object-edit. Image 1 is the edit target, the original Pomo tarot card CARD_ID. Produce a standalone full-bleed portrait illustration that will be displayed underneath a separate card frame. Remove the entire brown-and-gold ornamental picture frame, border books/stars/leaves, top number medallion and bottom parchment title plaque. Seamlessly reconstruct the scene into all removed border and plaque areas so painted scenery reaches every edge of a rectangular 2:3 canvas, ideally 1024x1536. Preserve the original scene, person's identity, hair, face, outfit, expression, pose, original tarot symbolism and props, their counts and arrangements, colors, lighting and painterly 3D illustration style. Do not redesign the scene or introduce extra people, symbols or objects. Keep the complete primary subject(s) and important props visible, positioned with breathing room for a later frame overlay. No ornamental border, no picture frame, no rounded card corners, no medallion, no parchment label, no lettering, no numbers, no title plaque, no UI elements, no watermarks. Opaque full painted backdrop, not a cutout. The only change is to remove the printed card frame and fill its former areas with continuation of the original illustration.",
  "numericSuitConstraint": "For number cards, the prompt also specifies the original suit prop count and arrangement.",
  "adjustments": [
    {
      "id": "pentacles-ten",
      "reason": "Keep all ten coins visible inside the common frame opening.",
      "constraint": "All coins within x=150..874 and y=200..600 on the 1024x1536 canvas."
    }
  ]
